+# Attempt account: vacuum-aware continuum control
+
+14 September 2026. Base: `fab69fdc4ac197159b8e6ae8d73a82bde2b20d55`.
+
+The aim is the four-dimensional Yang–Mills continuum mass gap. This route keeps the complete finite-link holonomy, interacting vacuum density, raw observable Gram matrices, and all comparison kernels. The inspected S6 section provides a concrete example of a smooth trivialization whose inverse retains its multiplying section; the new Yang–Mills local sections are constructed and verified directly, with their full curvature-energy cost.
+
+The completed calculations are an explicit smooth local right inverse at every finite-link configuration; the exact conditional-density derivative and three-square Dirichlet decomposition under refinement; a compatible projective equal-time vacuum limit; and an inverse-energy Schur budget with regulator-uniform infrared bounds. The regulator-state comparison is also constructed onto the reconstructed observable space. Its exact kernel retains escaping-label state sequences, and a commuting Walsh-observable fixture proves the need for the correction recorded in the preceding spectral note.
+
+The analytic statements are proved in [RESEARCH_NOTE.md](RESEARCH_NOTE.md). The independently executable [verify.py](verify.py) checks declared finite algebraic fixtures. The actual interacting vacuum densities and a positive continuum mass lower bound have not been numerically evaluated or proved by this contribution. No global-priority claim is made.
